## Letter from the CEO

Dear Stakeholders,

Fiscal Year 2022 was a year of aggressive growth as MedSync Health established itself as a leader in healthcare interoperability. We achieved revenue of $48.2 million, a 156% increase from the prior year, while making significant investments in our product portfolio and team.

This year we launched our third product, MedSync Analytics, and expanded internationally with offices in London and Berlin. Our Series B funding of $65M in March 2021 and Series C funding of $120M in August 2022 have provided us with the capital to execute on our ambitious growth plans.

Key highlights from FY 2022 include:

- **Revenue growth of 156%** to $48.2M
- **Launch of MedSync Analytics** in Q4 2022
- **International expansion** to London and Berlin
- **Series C funding** of $120M at $850M valuation
- **Team growth** to 485 employees

While we remain unprofitable as we invest in growth, our path to profitability is becoming clearer with improving gross margins and operating leverage.

Dr. Elena Rodriguez
Chief Executive Officer & Co-Founder

